# logrotate config for the bot's structured JSON log sink.
# Install on the VM at /etc/logrotate.d/diors-bot (root-owned, mode 644).
#
# Added 2026-07-28 15:34 EDT with the Cloud Logging overhaul. The sink is a plain append-only file, so
# without rotation it grows forever. Volume is genuinely small (the bot emits ~56 lines/day, and the
# whole journal was 35.7MB after 11 days), so this is about never having to think about it again
# rather than about reclaiming meaningful disk.
#
# `copytruncate` is deliberate: the bot holds an open write stream to this file and does NOT reopen on
# SIGHUP. A plain rename would leave it writing into the rotated-away inode forever — logs would just
# stop appearing, silently, which is the worst possible failure mode for the thing we built to make
# failures visible. copytruncate costs a brief copy and a tiny window where a line can be lost; that
# is the right trade here.

/home/harkirat/diors-builds/logs/app.log {
    daily
    rotate 14
    maxsize 50M
    copytruncate
    compress
    delaycompress
    missingok
    notifempty
    su harkirat harkirat
}
